The header of the 624bab3 stack's patch (patches/NativeMetal/0006-pages-identity-latch.patch), which says the what and the why:
| OneiOS take18, userland/metal/patches/NativeMetal/0006: a no-copy range's page identity without refused calls.
| Upstream: none (OneiOS; upstream NativeMetal 935c468's pages_identity is b0d6a07's).
| What: bridge/NativeMetalObjects.rs pages_identity asks mach_vm_region_recurse until a status other than KERN_SUCCESS or
| KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS comes back (a sandbox's MIG filter); that refusal is latched and the call is not made again in the
| process. The identity then comes from mach_vm_region: VM_REGION_TOP_INFO's object id and VM_REGION_BASIC_INFO_64's
| offset, hashed as before. Neither flavor walks the entry's pages (xnu-12377 vm_map_region; proc_pidinfo's
| PROC_PIDREGIONINFO would walk every page of the entry, fill_procregioninfo -> vm_map_region_walk). The top info's id is the
| bottom object of the shadow chain (vm_map_region_top_walk), the recursion's the entry's own: they are the same object only
| where the entry has no shadow and needs no copy, which the share mode says (not SM_COW, not SM_EMPTY); elsewhere, and for a
| submap entry, the answer is None: a remap, the old (correct, costly) answer. A refusal of mach_vm_region is latched too.
| Why: WebKit's GPU process may not call mach_vm_region_recurse (its kernel MIG filter allows mach_vm_region: WebKit's iOS
| gpu-defines.sb lists mach_vm_region_recurse only for ASAN builds): take17's log has 20,018 "deny(1) syscall-mig 319"
| (kobject index 319 = MIG 4815 mach_vm_region_recurse), two at every no-copy buffer, and each refusal made the range
| "remapped": host_range_remapped and a new import of the pages for every no-copy buffer of the process.
| Switch: boot argument oneios-region-identity=0 (ONEIOS_REGION_IDENTITY=0): no second source (every such range a remap, as
| before, but without the refused calls). Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=pages-identity-latch). The telemetry row
| "N no-copy ranges checked C remapped R" says the effect (R near C in the GPU process before).

